# Stale Hooks Warning Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Widen reach and improve clarity of the stale-hooks warning. Fire it on every visible `entire` subcommand (not just `status` / `enable`), and rewrite the message so it states the action to take without jargon.

**Architecture:** One new file `cmd/entire/cli/drift_warning.go` splits the behavior into three pure pieces — `shouldSkipDriftWarning(cmd)` predicate, `emitStaleHooksWarning(w, drifts)` renderer, and a thin `driftWarningPreRun` wrapper attached to root as `PersistentPreRun`. Existing inline warnings in `status.go` and `setup.go` are replaced by calls to the shared renderer so the message is rendered in exactly one place.

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, cobra, lipgloss (via existing `statusStyles`), `golang.org/x/mod/semver` (indirect via `agent.CheckHookDrift`).

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-24-stale-hooks-warning-design.md`

